# Every checkout has the same bytes.
#
# Git hands a Windows working tree CRLF unless told otherwise, and this
# repository puts text inside the programs it builds: the whitepaper, the
# website and both locales go into cairn-explorer through include_str!. So the
# same commit built on Windows served different bytes than the same commit
# built on Linux, for a reason that has nothing to do with the code, and a test
# comparing a published figure against the sentence stating it failed there and
# only there, on a sentence that happened to wrap.
#
# Every file under version control here is text and is already stored with LF,
# so this renormalises nothing. It changes what Windows is given.
* text=auto eol=lf
